        <!-- ============================ HERO ============================ -->
<section class="hero">
  <div class="hero-grid">
    <div class="hero-copy reveal">
      <a class="pill" href="https://github.com/basiltt/xstate-statemachine-rs/releases/tag/v0.1.0">
        <span class="pill-dot"></span>
        v0.1.0 is out &mdash; release notes
        <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 3l5 5-5 5"/></svg>
      </a>
      <h1>
        <span class="h1-line">State machines</span>
        <span class="h1-line">for Rust,</span>
        <span class="h1-line h1-grad">blazing fast.</span>
      </h1>
      <p class="hero-lede">
        Run your XState v5 or Stately JSON unmodified, or declare statecharts with declarative Rust macros.
        Sub-microsecond transitions (69.8 ns p50) with 0 steady-state heap allocations. Tokio actors, durable persistence,
        transactional outbox EDA, and Stately Studio visual inspection. 15 modular workspace crates.
      </p>
      <div class="hero-actions">
        <a href="guide/getting-started.html" class="btn btn-primary">
          Get started
          <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 8h10M9 4l4 4-4 4"/></svg>
        </a>
        <a href="https://docs.rs/xstate-statemachine" class="btn btn-glass" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read the API</a>
      </div>
      <div class="hero-install" role="group" aria-label="Install command">
        <code><span class="prompt">$</span> cargo add xstate-statemachine</code>
        <button class="copy-btn" type="button" data-copy="cargo add xstate-statemachine" aria-label="Copy install command">
          <svg class="ic-copy" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M0 6.75C0 5.784.784 5 1.75 5h1.5a.75.75 0 010 1.5h-1.5a.25.25 0 00-.25.25v7.5c0 .138.112.25.25.25h7.5a.25.25 0 00.25-.25v-1.5a.75.75 0 011.5 0v1.5A1.75 1.75 0 019.25 16h-7.5A1.75 1.75 0 010 14.25zM5 1.75C5 .784 5.784 0 6.75 0h7.5C15.216 0 16 .784 16 1.75v7.5A1.75 1.75 0 0114.25 11h-7.5A1.75 1.75 0 015 9.25zm1.75-.25a.25.25 0 00-.25.25v7.5c0 .138.112.25.25.25h7.5a.25.25 0 00.25-.25v-7.5a.25.25 0 00-.25-.25z"/></svg>
          <svg class="ic-check" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 8.5l3 3 7-7"/></svg>
        </button>
      </div>
      <ul class="hero-trust" aria-label="At a glance">
        <li><strong>69.8 ns</strong> p50 transitions</li>
        <li><strong>0</strong> heap allocs</li>
        <li><strong>15</strong> workspace crates</li>
        <li><strong>MIT</strong> licensed</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <figure class="hero-machine reveal reveal-delay" id="heroMachine" aria-label="An order-lifecycle state machine, animating through its states">
      <div class="machine-chrome">
        <span class="dot dot-r"></span><span class="dot dot-y"></span><span class="dot dot-g"></span>
        <span class="machine-title">order.machine.json</span>
        <span class="machine-live"><span class="live-dot"></span>live</span>
      </div>
      <svg viewBox="0 0 520 320" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" role="img">
        <defs>
          <linearGradient id="gEdge" x1="0" x2="1"><stop offset="0" stop-color="#10B981"/><stop offset="1" stop-color="#2DD4BF"/></linearGradient>
          <radialGradient id="gNode" cx="50%" cy="40%" r="60%"><stop offset="0" stop-color="#6EE7B7"/><stop offset="1" stop-color="#10B981"/></radialGradient>
          <marker id="arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse"><path d="M0 0L10 5 0 10z" class="edge-arrow"/></marker>
          <marker id="arrowOn" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse"><path d="M0 0L10 5 0 10z" class="edge-arrow-on"/></marker>
          <filter id="glow" x="-80%" y="-80%" width="260%" height="260%"><feGaussianBlur stdDeviation="8" result="b"/><feMerge><feMergeNode in="b"/><feMergeNode in="b"/><feMergeNode in="SourceGraphic"/></feMerge></filter>
        </defs>

        <path class="edge" data-edge="pending-submitted"  d="M100 80 H 220" marker-end="url(#arrow)"/>
        <path class="edge" data-edge="submitted-open"     d="M300 80 H 420" marker-end="url(#arrow)"/>
        <path class="edge" data-edge="open-filled"        d="M460 120 V 200" marker-end="url(#arrow)"/>
        <path class="edge" data-edge="open-cancelled"     d="M432 106 L 328 214" marker-end="url(#arrow)"/>
        <path class="edge" data-edge="submitted-rejected" d="M260 120 V 200" marker-end="url(#arrow)"/>

        <text class="edge-event" id="heroEvent" x="0" y="0" text-anchor="middle"></text>
        <circle class="edge-pulse" id="heroPulse" r="6"/>

        <g class="node" data-state="pending"   transform="translate(60,80)"><circle class="halo" r="46"/><circle r="38"/><text dy="4">pending</text></g>
        <g class="node" data-state="submitted" transform="translate(260,80)"><circle class="halo" r="46"/><circle r="38"/><text dy="4">submitted</text></g>
        <g class="node" data-state="open"      transform="translate(460,80)"><circle class="halo" r="46"/><circle r="38"/><text dy="4">open</text></g>
        <g class="node node-final" data-state="filled"    transform="translate(460,240)"><circle class="halo" r="46"/><circle r="38"/><circle r="31" class="final-ring"/><text dy="4">filled</text></g>
        <g class="node node-final" data-state="cancelled" transform="translate(300,240)"><circle class="halo" r="46"/><circle r="38"/><circle r="31" class="final-ring"/><text dy="4">cancelled</text></g>
        <g class="node node-final" data-state="rejected"  transform="translate(260,240)" style="display:none"><circle class="halo" r="46"/><circle r="38"/><circle r="31" class="final-ring"/><text dy="4">rejected</text></g>
      </svg>
      <figcaption>
        <span>state <code id="heroState">pending</code></span>
        <span>event <code id="heroLastEvent">&mdash;</code></span>
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============================ BENTO ============================ -->
<section class="bento-section">
  <div class="section-head reveal">
    <h2>Everything a statechart runtime should do.<br><span class="muted">Nothing it shouldn't.</span></h2>
  </div>

  <div class="bento">
    <article class="card card-lg reveal">
      <div class="card-glow" style="--gx:20%;--gy:0%"></div>
      <h3>Sub-Microsecond Zero-Allocation Fast Path</h3>
      <p>Plain microsteps execute in <strong>69.8 ns p50</strong> (&gt;14.3M ops/s) with <strong>0 heap allocations</strong>. Active states use <code>FixedBitSet</code>; identifiers use stack-inlined <code>SmolStr</code>; transition actions execute inline with <code>SmallVec</code>.</p>
      <pre class="mini"><code>use xstate_statemachine::prelude::*;
let mut door = SyncInterpreter::new(machine, logic);
door.start()?;
let changed = door.send_fast("OPEN")?; // 69.8 ns transition
assert!(changed);</code></pre>
    </article>

    <article class="card reveal">
      <div class="card-glow" style="--gx:80%;--gy:0%"></div>
      <div class="card-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M13 2 3 14h9l-1 8 10-12h-9z"/></svg></div>
      <h3>XState v5 &amp; Stately Compatible</h3>
      <p>Load JSON exported from Stately Studio directly into Rust without modification. 53 conformance fixtures verify 100% parity against Node XState.</p>
    </article>

    <article class="card reveal">
      <div class="card-glow" style="--gx:50%;--gy:100%"></div>
      <div class="card-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M12 3l8 3v6c0 5-3.5 8-8 9-4.5-1-8-4-8-9V6z"/><path d="m9 12 2 2 4-4"/></svg></div>
      <h3><a href="guide/tokio.html">Tokio Actors &amp; Mailboxes</a></h3>
      <p>Spawn actors as Tokio tasks with bounded mailboxes, backpressure policies (<code>Block</code>, <code>DropNewest</code>, <code>Error</code>), and precision cancel-safe timers.</p>
    </article>

    <article class="card reveal">
      <div class="card-glow" style="--gx:0%;--gy:50%"></div>
      <div class="card-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><circle cx="12" cy="13" r="8"/><path d="M12 9v4l3 2M9 2h6"/></svg></div>
      <h3>Virtual Clock Testing</h3>
      <p><code>SimulatedClock</code> advances virtual time instantaneously. Test a 72-hour saga or 30-day billing trial deterministically in 2 milliseconds without sleeping.</p>
    </article>

    <article class="card card-wide reveal">
      <div class="card-glow" style="--gx:100%;--gy:50%"></div>
      <h3>Ask, Don't Poll</h3>
      <p><code>actor.send_and_wait("PAY", Duration::from_secs(5)).await</code> awaits the statechart transition and returns a typed <code>Receipt</code> the moment the microstep completes.</p>
      <div class="receipt">
        <span class="receipt-k">Receipt</span>
        <span>state_ids=<b>["order.paid"]</b></span>
        <span>unhandled=<b>false</b></span>
        <span>actions_executed=<b>2</b></span>
        <span>duration=<b>70ns</b></span>
      </div>
    </article>

    <article class="card reveal">
      <div class="card-glow" style="--gx:50%;--gy:0%"></div>
      <div class="card-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><ellipse cx="12" cy="5" rx="8" ry="3"/><path d="M4 5v14c0 1.7 3.6 3 8 3s8-1.3 8-3V5"/><path d="M4 12c0 1.7 3.6 3 8 3s8-1.3 8-3"/></svg></div>
      <h3><a href="guide/persistence.html">Durable Persistence</a></h3>
      <p>Durable stores for SQLite, PostgreSQL, Redis, and File. Layout <code>v4</code> binary snapshots with 16-hex character topology hashes compatible with the Python library.</p>
    </article>

    <article class="card reveal">
      <div class="card-glow" style="--gx:0%;--gy:50%"></div>
      <div class="card-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M12 2l8 4v6c0 5-3.5 8.5-8 10-4.5-1.5-8-5-8-10V6z"/><path d="M9 12l2 2 4-4"/></svg></div>
      <h3><a href="guide/axum.html">Axum Web &amp; Live Inspector</a></h3>
      <p>Expose statecharts as REST APIs, Server-Sent Events (SSE), or WebSockets via Axum. Connect the Stately Studio Inspector live over WebSocket/SSE to visualize in real time.</p>
    </article>

    <article class="card reveal">
      <div class="card-glow" style="--gx:100%;--gy:0%"></div>
      <div class="card-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M4 12h4l2-6 4 12 2-6h4"/></svg></div>
      <h3><a href="guide/eda.html">Transactional Outbox EDA</a></h3>
      <p>CloudEvents 1.0 messaging with atomic outbox commits. Native adapters for NATS JetStream, RabbitMQ, AWS SQS, and Redis Streams with dead-letter queue (DLQ) support.</p>
    </article>

    <article class="card reveal">
      <div class="card-glow" style="--gx:0%;--gy:0%"></div>
      <div class="card-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="3"/><path d="M2 12s3.5-7 10-7 10 7 10 7-3.5 7-10 7S2 12 2 12z"/></svg></div>
      <h3><a href="guide/observability.html">Prometheus Observability</a></h3>
      <p>Clean metric emissions via the <code>metrics</code> facade: transition rates, step latencies, queue depths, error counters, and active actor gauges with strict label hygiene.</p>
    </article>

    <article class="card reveal">
      <div class="card-glow" style="--gx:50%;--gy:100%"></div>
      <div class="card-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M4 4h16M4 20h16M7 4c0 8 10 8 10 16M17 4c0 8-10 8-10 16"/></svg></div>
      <h3><a href="guide/macros.html">Proc Macro DSL</a></h3>
      <p><code>#[derive(TypedEvent)]</code>, <code>#[derive(TypedState)]</code>, and the <code>statechart!</code> DSL give you compile-time type-checked transitions without runtime string typos.</p>
    </article>

    <article class="card reveal">
      <div class="card-glow" style="--gx:0%;--gy:100%"></div>
      <div class="card-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><rect x="3" y="4" width="18" height="16" rx="2"/><path d="M7 9l3 3-3 3M13 15h4"/></svg></div>
      <h3><a href="guide/cli.html">The `xsm` Companion CLI</a></h3>
      <p>Run <code>xsm validate</code> on your JSON charts, <code>xsm diagram</code> to export Mermaid/PlantUML, <code>xsm inspect --live</code> to bridge to Stately, and <code>xsm simulate</code> to walk paths.</p>
    </article>

    <article class="card reveal">
      <div class="card-glow" style="--gx:100%;--gy:100%"></div>
      <div class="card-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M9 3h6M10 3v6l-5.5 9A2 2 0 0 0 6.2 21h11.6a2 2 0 0 0 1.7-3L14 9V3"/><path d="M8 15h8"/></svg></div>
      <h3><a href="guide/patterns.html">Resilience &amp; Sagas</a></h3>
      <p>Distributed saga orchestrator with automated backward compensation rollbacks. Full-jitter exponential backoff, circuit breakers, and idempotency key caches.</p>
    </article>

    <article class="card reveal">
      <div class="card-glow" style="--gx:50%;--gy:50%"></div>
      <div class="card-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><rect x="5" y="8" width="14" height="11" rx="2"/><path d="M12 4v4M9 13h.01M15 13h.01M9 16h6"/></svg></div>
      <h3><a href="guide/agents.html">LLM Agent Guardrails</a></h3>
      <p>The model proposes actions; the statechart decides what is permitted. Enforce per-state tool allow-lists, token budget guards, and durable human approvals.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============================ CODE SHOWCASE ============================ -->
<section class="code-showcase">
  <div class="section-head reveal">
    <h2>Define in JSON, Macros, or Dynamic Code</h2>
    <p class="section-subtitle">Pick the style that matches your project. All compile to the same sub-microsecond runtime.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="code-tabs reveal">
